-# @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-skill-settings
-
-English | [中文](README.zh.md)
-
-Web Settings page for Harness-local Skill modes. The client reads the active session's complete Skill catalog, including entries hidden from `/`, and the `skill-settings` settings namespace. It renders enabled, manual-only, and disabled choices, then writes only that namespace through the existing settings wire.
-
-The page shows author-owned restrictions separately. Selecting enabled never widens those restrictions because the Host registry intersects local modes with `SKILL.md` frontmatter. A rejected write keeps the previous view and a retry reloads the catalog and settings document.
-
-## Model Experience
-
-None directly. The page changes Host settings; the Host controls future model catalogs and user-invocation checks.
-
-#### KV Cache effect
-
-None in the browser. A saved model-visible change may make the Host publish the normal replacement Skill catalog on a later agent step.
-
-## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
-
-- **Active-project view** — the page requires an open project session and lists the Skill winners for that session's cwd and preset.
-- **No bulk editing** — modes are changed one Skill at a time; search, grouping, and reset of stale stored names are deferred.
